            <ArticleTitle>Symptomatic bipartite patella: three subtypes, three representative cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S72-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1055/s-0032-1313746</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bipartite patella can be classified into three unique subtypes; type I, II, and III. The following case series describes three representative cases of each subtype and a spectrum of location-specific treatment options for surgical care of the symptomatic bipartite patella.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Thieme Medical Publishers 333 Seventh Avenue, New York, NY 10001, USA.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
